  triage:title "herdr_queue_wake.rs reminder-pacing test failures are a BA.3 stale-base artifact, not a BA.4 or BA.5 regression" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (converged: quality-mgr, ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-BA4-F001, req-qa ATM-QA-002, arch-qa ARCH-001, rust-qa-agent QA-001), PR #1408 @ 5ab184d75, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5642703785 -- and independently rediscovered on PR #1407 @ b617a9eab (11 of 13 tests there are a separate BA.5-introduced issue, but ac02_seventeen_due_reminders_split_across_ticks_at_sixteen and ax5_09_generic_emit_failure_counts_and_respects_cooldown are this identical failure, per https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642789392, see BA5-QA1-001). cargo test -p atm-http-runtime --lib fails these 2 tests on both 5ab184d75 and b617a9eab: ac02_... panics at herdr_queue_wake.rs:2512 (left==right failed: left 16, right 1); ax5_09_... panics at herdr_queue_wake.rs:2583 (cooldown suppresses a retry, left 2, right 1). fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5642738654, corroborated at https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642806916): both tests fail identically on a clean export of the shared BA.3 merge point 19816c821 alone -- git diff 19816c821..5ab184d75 for herdr_queue_wake.rs/herdr_queue_wake_reminders.rs is empty, so this is BA.3's own MemberObservation/still_idle() work, not a BA.4 or BA.5 regression. Resolution: arch-ctm's final BA.3 sha must have both tests green; solar/cipher merge that sha forward once fenix relays it. No BA.4 or BA.5 code change." ;
